{
  "description": "Rows that exercise the SEPARATOR COUNT path: a 0xab consumed as a PUSHDATA length byte in a script whose walk also stops early, so the walk's separator count and a naive count of 0xab bytes give different declared lengths.",
  "whyThisExists": "The sibling fixture sighash-codesep-undecodable.json is node-judged and stays entirely GREEN when the walk's separator count is replaced by a naive count of every 0xab byte. In this library the declared length has TWO derivations: when the walk stops early it is set explicitly as len(suffix) - separators_reached, and when the walk reaches the end it comes from the stripped script's own length via chunk-level removeCodeseparators. Those always agree, but a sabotage of one is invisible to rows served by the other. No body in that fixture has a 0xab in a length field AND an early stop, so every one of its rows takes the stripped-length route for that question. These bodies have both.",
  "sabotageCoverage": {
    "naiveByteCountForTheWalk": "breaks 12 of the 12 original-algorithm rows here; breaks 0 of the 48 rows in sighash-codesep-undecodable.json",
    "byteLevelExcisionInsteadOfChunkLevel": "breaks 4 rows of sighash-codesep-undecodable.json (4d01ab and ab4dab00 at both original hash types); breaks 0 rows here",
    "conclusion": "the two fixtures guard the two routes and neither covers the other's"
  },
  "provenance": {
    "rowsAuthoredBy": "this project - bodies chosen here specifically to make the two counts diverge, with no expected values",
    "rowsMd5": "2a3306e9d64dda275f9472feac9df2d7",
    "expectedValuesFrom": "the nts frontier session, 2026-10-16",
    "emitters": [
