    "witnessCaveat": "As with the sibling fixture the two emitters' output files are byte-identical, which for a deterministic function in one output format is what agreement looks like; the two-witness claim rests on the distinct binary hashes above. Both run by one operator, one machine.",
    "independentlyJoined": "Joined against a FRESH run of this library: 48 comparisons (24 rows x 2 emitters), 0 preimage differences, 0 digest differences, every digest confirmed as sha256d of its own preimage.",
    "headline": "ab6a4eababab declares 5, not 2: a 0xab the walk has already consumed as part of a length field is not a separator and is not counted."
